本書逐章研讀彼得前書全書五章，並附索引與參考資料附錄，整合老弟兄一貫的查經方法論與以基督為中心的框架（本書並無對應之老弟兄彼得前書逐節查經筆記原始記錄，此為誠實說明，詳見附錄），alongside John MacArthur 逐節解經講道，以及 G. Campbell Morgan 的屬靈與結構分析。全信的軌跡，從重生得著活潑的盼望、到蒙召作聖潔的祭司、到客旅在世如何順服見證、到為義受苦如同有分於基督的苦難、直到長老牧養群羊、抵擋魔鬼、儆醒等候——彼得寫給分散各地、正受火煉之試驗的客旅最貼身的一封信，在這裡逐章展開。

{\baskervillefont\color{CoverCream} chapter-by-chapter study of all five chapters of 1 Peter, with index and references appendices, integrating the Elder's documented Bible-study methodology and Christ-centered theological framework (this book has no corresponding verse-by-verse Elder teaching notes on 1 Peter itself --- an honest disclosure detailed in the appendix), alongside John MacArthur's verse-by-verse exposition and G. Campbell Morgan's spiritual and structural analysis. The letter's arc unfolds chapter by chapter: from new birth into a living hope, through the call to be a holy priesthood, through the sojourner's submission and witness in the world, through suffering for righteousness as a share in Christ's own suffering, to elders shepherding the flock, resisting the devil, and staying watchful --- Peter's most intimate letter to scattered sojourners under fiery trial, traced here in full.}
$endif$
\end{minipage}

